   "newText": "Evidence is one demo and one accepted test; the source panel location varied between them, supporting a position-independent rule.\n\n## Additional confirmed instance evidence (2026-09-29)\nA separate instance with the same task ID was solved and accepted, further confirming the rule:\n\n- Demo input/output was 13x15, background 8, separator color 1. Full separator row 6 and column 7 define four 6x7 panels. Source was lower-right (rows 7–12, columns 8–14); its entire 6x7 pattern, including background-colored cells, was copied to all four panels. The separator lines remained unchanged.\n- Test input was 29x20, background 9, separator color 2. Full separator rows 9 and 19 and columns 6 and 13 define a 3x3 array of 9x6 tiles. The only populated tile was bottom-left (rows 20–28, columns 0–5). It was copied exactly to all nine panel locations; separators remained intact. The submission was accepted with zero wrong attempts.\n\nThis independently confirms that all equal-sized panels receive the one nonblank tile, not only blank panels, and that the source can occupy a non-top-left location. When extracting a tile, preserve every cell value exactly (including the apparent background value); replicate its local coordinates in each panel."
